& [Finding]
  + P0 Revision 0.2 already owns strict closure declaration replay graph order targets expected receipt denials and zero-effect verification
  + no current contract converts the exact P0 graph into one closed ordered future material-work surface while keeping execution authority false
  + the smallest reusable input is exact canonical P0 envelope bytes, not an ambient repository file list or observed host

& [ReusableSubstrate]
  + cantor_core::runtime_closure provides strict parsing validation deterministic compilation topological order source-kind distinctions expected receipt and exact twenty-five denials
  + seeded compiler build candidate and receipt forms may inform field design only by exact identity and cannot be relabeled as materialization
  + succeeding-SOP and self-work plans demonstrate proposed-only operation contracts but carry unrelated authority and are not imported semantically

& [SelectedBoundary]
  + compile one effectless MaterializationPlanRequest from exact P0 envelope bytes into nine ordered phases and thirteen closed operation kinds
  + every planned operation is unresolved proposed_awaiting_separate_commission and carries only required-but-denied future capabilities
  + actual RIS-P1 executor host profile artifact resolver filesystem process verification rollback receipt and activation remain separate

& [BlockersPreserved]
  + no admitted bootstrap executable real installation SOP closure host tuple artifact pack toolchain dependency vendor model bytes license acceptance or secret custody input is currently supplied
  + therefore the first fixture must remain synthetic_provider_free and cannot be reported as a real installation plan

& [Disposition]
  + source is sufficient for provider-free formation with strict upstream replay and zero effects
  + no Rust until canonical signature formation manifest verifier publication and post-push bookend complete
